{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794490957,"nonce":"xdnBuMsZWQjHBI9cFLvlWcMWuTw=","message":"Local commits ec886869 and 387983ec (not pushed): opacity and effect groups, and the text in them, move on rows.\n\nOn rows now: translate, scale, turn and fade of a node and of nodes nested four deep; the text under them, sharp at rest and after it settles; text-only nodes; a node's own clip and its ancestors'; group opacity (set on the layer command) and layer effects; text captured inside a group.\n\nStill a full repaint of the frame while the value moves (the compositor's patch result is one bool, so each is all or nothing):\n- an image or an SVG inside a bound node. Rows move primitives and glyphs; images and SVGs are drawn apart from the batch and would stay where they were painted. Needs the image and SVG passes to read the table.\n- a group that has to keep its place in the paint order: a glass group, one with an image or SVG inside, and one that content painted after it lies over (any stream) at rest. These stay in the static batch. A group that goes dynamic draws above later static content if it moves over it, as a plain moving node does; tree order there needs a split static layer.\n- blend-mode and 3D layers; a non-uniform scale with a turn; a turn over a clip that has to move; a clip that is not a rectangle and moves; chains deeper than four; two groups pushed with the same configuration (cannot be told apart); CSS animations and transitions, which are not on the table.\n\nHarness: every scene is now held to the vector paint on the table path, not only the ones that must be on rows. New scenes: a tile painted after the card, a foreground group, an image, a fading image, a layer effect. A scene waits for background loads before it starts, three identical frames in a row.\n\nA bug found on the way: a node painted again for the foreground stream got a second ordinal, so only its foreground child had a slot and the card stayed put. It keeps its first.\n\nSuites green with the table off and on: blinc_app 377 (ignored included), blinc_recorder 309, blinc_gpu, blinc_layout and blinc_core 1333. blinc_test_suite has 2 failures at a clean HEAD too (TestHarness::new) and a third against a gitignored golden from December that a clean HEAD fails the same way; not touched.\n\nTimings (what_a_frame_costs_with_many_bound_cards, ignored, headless offscreen on the dev Mac, median ms per frame including the render and read back, which every path pays; noisy, two runs agree to within about 20%). Grid of small cards, each with its own translate, scale and label, all moving:\n  10 cards:  promoted full 5 to 11, vectors full 5 to 8, promoted patched 4 to 6, node table 3 to 4\n  40 cards:  promoted full 13 to 18, vectors full 6 to 7, promoted patched 10 to 12, node table 3\n  140 cards: promoted full 24 to 28, vectors full 7 to 11, promoted patched 24 to 28, node table 5\n  140 cards at 2x density: promoted full 42, vectors full 11, promoted patched 37, node table 8\nThe table's frame stays flat as cards are added; the promoted paths grow with the card count. Still to measure: a window with a real compositor and display, and the P0 benchmark on the phones.","files":null}]}